{#- The glyphs the box and the thread draw, once, for `<use>` to point at.

    §7 in four strokes: a 16px viewBox, no fill, `currentColor` at 1.4, round caps —
    line diagrams of what they do. The `+` beside them is not here on purpose: §7 keeps
    typed characters as themselves, and a plus is one.

    Since 2026-09-10 the box's three actions are drawn rather than written — a
    microphone, an arrow, a loudspeaker — with the word kept as the control's label,
    so what a screen reader says is what the button used to say. The sprite is zero by
    zero and off the page rather than `hidden`: a `display: none` sprite is one some
    browsers will not draw a `<use>` from. -#}
